Added `enqueueMany` to `src/queue.js` with an up-front `items.length + newItems.length > capacity` check, so overflow throws `QueueFullError` before any push and the queue is untouched. Added tests in `test/queue.test.js` covering in-order append plus return size, exact fit, atomic overflow (size and head preserved, nothing partially appended), and empty-array no-ops. `node --test` passes 33/33, and no other files changed.
